## Bug Fix & Issue Resolution (MANDATORY)

When the user reports a **bug**, **issue**, **regression**, or asks to **fix** something broken, read **before coding**:

1. `AGENT_BUG_FIX_RULEBOOK.md` - Universal workflow, guardrails, and checklist (any agent, any issue)
2. `AGENTS.md` - This project's contracts and page ownership
3. `SMALL_BUG_FIX_PLAN.md` - This project's bug catalog (open vs fixed)

Shortcut pointer: `BUG_FIX_RULE_GUIDE.md`. Always-on: `.agents/rules/bug-fix.md`.

## Auto-Knowledge Graph

Before starting work, ALWAYS read these files first:

1. `AGENTS.md` - Agent rules and auto-update instructions
2. `.understand-anything/knowledge-graph.json` - Full project architecture (274 nodes, 338 edges)
3. `.understand-anything/PROJECT_AUDIT.md` - Human-readable project audit

## After Code Changes

Run this command to keep the knowledge graph updated:
```bash
node scripts/quick-update.mjs
```

This takes ~30 seconds and updates the project map.
